plugin.json version: 0.1.0  (all runs preload evals/helpers/no-network.mjs; any attempt prints NETWORK-ATTEMPT)
$ lib/verify/check-cuts.mjs --help
check-cuts — check that every cut lands inside a silent gap

Usage: check-cuts [options] <file>

Cuts come from --cuts (ms) or from scene detection. A cut passes when it sits inside a silence (audio at or below --noise-db) lasting at least --min-silence-ms. Exit 0 if all pass, 1 if any fails (failing timecodes are listed).

Options:
      --min-silence-ms    Minimum silent gap a cut must sit in (default: 300)
      --cuts <ms,ms,...>  Cut times in ms (skips scene detection)
      --scene-threshold   Scene-change threshold for detected cuts (default: 0.02)
      --noise-db          Silence threshold (default: -40)
      --json              Print the result as JSON
  -h, --help              Show this help and exit
      --version           Print the plugin version and exit

Examples:
  check-cuts review.mp4 --min-silence-ms 300
  check-cuts spine/narration.wav --cuts 6500,14000 --min-silence-ms 400
exit=0
